          "distinct": true,
          "id": "d4a9ea116cf2c7b0867b6165a3cf85cf3d13f6f6",
          "message": "feat(cli): shell completion for archive args, flags, and output formats (#126)\n\n* feat(cli): shell completion for archive args, flags, and output formats\n\nCobra already auto-generates the `completion` subcommand for bash, zsh,\nfish, and PowerShell, so subcommand and `--flag` names complete out of the\nbox. This wires up the value-level completion that wasn't covered:\n\n- positional `<capture.kshrk>` args (inspect/open/ui/transitions) and the\n  archive-valued flags (--in/--out/--before/--after/--archive) now complete\n  to `*.kshrk` files only\n- `--config` completes to YAML files (registered on the root persistent flag)\n- `-o/--output` completes to the valid choices per command\n  (inspect: table|json|yaml, transitions: table|json, diff: text|json)\n\nAdds a shell-completion install section to docs/usage.md, plus cmd tests\ndriving Cobra's `__complete` entry point. The help-examples test now skips\nhidden commands so the `__complete` helper doesn't trip it.\n\nRefs #32\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(cli): address Copilot review on shell completion\n\n- capture --output: replace MarkFlagFilename with a custom completion func\n  so \"-\" (NDJSON to stdout) is still offered while file completion stays\n  scoped to *.kshrk\n- completion tests: parse the ShellCompDirective and assert the\n  FilterFileExt/NoFileComp bits instead of a fragile string-suffix check\n- completion tests: cover capture --output (incl. the \"-\" stdout case) and\n  --config YAML scoping (root persistent flag + redact --config)\n- docs/usage.md: list capture --output among the *.kshrk-scoped flags\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
