          "message": "docs: formalize the .kshrk format-compatibility guarantee (#115) (#129)\n\n* docs: formalize the .kshrk format-compatibility guarantee\n\nCloses #115.\n\nExpand the \"Format version & compatibility\" section of archive-format.md into\nan explicit stability promise for v1.0:\n- Defines the contract surface (entry layout + JSON schemas + pathDir/seq\n  derivation) and what is explicitly NOT contractual (ZIP method, entry order,\n  timestamps, byte size) so we can keep optimizing encoding.\n- States the evolution rules (additive vs version-bumping) and the\n  ignore-unknowns requirement for consumers.\n- States the reader compatibility promise: a MAJOR reads all format_versions\n  <= its own; pre-versioning archives are v1; newer archives are refused.\n- Adds a contributor note: a breaking change must bump CurrentFormatVersion,\n  update this section, and extend the golden-fixture test.\n\nCross-links the guarantee from the README docs table.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: clarify non-contractual ZIP method and per-entry compression\n\nAddress review on the compatibility guarantee:\n- Note Deflate-stored archives are equally valid (the writer just stores the\n  already-Zstd payloads, but method is non-contractual either way).\n- Clarify only *.json.zst entries are Zstd-compressed; metadata.json is plain\n  JSON, so readers shouldn't blindly Zstd-decode every entry.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T19:12:05-04:00",
