          "distinct": true,
          "id": "89dacb22d799f54149c1aed9a95a5a271e592076",
          "message": "feat(diagnose): findings engine + kshrk diagnose CLI (#131)\n\n* feat(diagnose): findings engine + kshrk diagnose CLI\n\nPart of #111. Adds an offline diagnostic pass that turns a capture's raw\nstate into severity-ranked findings.\n\n- New internal/diagnose package: Finding/Report schema (with SchemaVersion\n  for the stable -o json contract), an engine, and rules. ClassifyPod /\n  PodHealth move here from internal/ui/v2 (aliased back, so v2 is unchanged)\n  so the CLI and UI share one classifier.\n- Rules (the #111 acceptance set): pod health (CrashLoopBackOff, OOMKilled,\n  image-pull, container/config errors, Failed/Unknown), unschedulable pods\n  (with reason), unbound PVCs, and control-plane/node version skew. Findings\n  group by owner+reason with a count, and degrade gracefully when inputs\n  weren't captured.\n- New `kshrk diagnose <capture.kshrk>`: table/json/yaml output, --at,\n  --severity, --category, and --fail-on <severity> for CI gating (reuses the\n  diff exitError).\n- Tests: engine rules over a fixture (all rules, grouping, severity/category\n  filters) + CLI tests (json shape, --fail-on exit code, validation).\n\nFollow-ups (per the #111 plan): dashboard Diagnostics view + unify the\noverview Issues panel (PR 3), and docs/-o json schema reference (PR 4).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(diagnose): address review on PR 1\n\n- scheduling.unschedulable: include the pod owner in the grouping key so\n  distinct workloads with the same generic message aren't merged.\n- storage.pvc-unbound: key per claim (ns+name) so distinct PVCs aren't\n  collapsed into one finding.\n- SeverityAtLeast: reject unknown severities (no silent rank-0 match).\n- diagnose --at: reject times outside the capture window instead of\n  silently reconstructing 404s and reporting \"No findings\".\n- Tests for each fix.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
