          "distinct": true,
          "id": "56cfa26d04d1737e866c1422f622cda15efc030a",
          "message": "feat(diagnose): add workload/node/cluster rules (PR 2) (#132)\n\nPart of #111. Builds on the engine from PR 1 (#131) with more rules:\n\n- workload.no-requests (warning) / workload.no-limits (info) — containers\n  missing resource requests/limits, grouped by owner.\n- workload.replicas-unavailable (warning) — Deployment/StatefulSet/\n  ReplicaSet ready<desired, and DaemonSet numberReady<desired.\n- node.not-ready (critical) and node.pressure (warning) — node Ready=False\n  and Disk/Memory/PIDPressure conditions.\n- cluster.deprecated-api (warning) — index-driven detection of\n  removed/deprecated group/versions (extensions/v1beta1, batch/v1beta1\n  CronJob, policy/v1beta1, autoscaling/v2beta*, …); no body reads needed.\n\nTests cover each new rule plus the index-only deprecated-API path.\n\nStill to come: event↔object↔log correlation (PR 2b), then the dashboard\nDiagnostics view (PR 3) and docs (PR 4).",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-28T02:32:35-04:00",
          "tree_id": "7984ad6e4537cfeaece2730ffc0905c4d3c6c1ae",
