          "distinct": true,
          "id": "3551ff887327da168bde13bf9196e9d3c758a2e7",
          "message": "docs: diagnose command, rules, and JSON schema (#111, PR 4) (#134)\n\n* docs: document the diagnose command, rules, and JSON schema\n\nPart of #111 (PR 4).\n\n- usage.md: new \"Diagnose\" section — CLI usage/flags, table example,\n  --fail-on CI gating, the full rule catalog (rule_id/severity/category),\n  and the stable -o json schema (pinned by schema_version).\n- web-ui.md: a \"Diagnostics\" section describing the dashboard view.\n- README: add diagnose as a third step in \"How it works\".\n\n* docs(web-ui): correct the stale replay-memory caveat\n\n#116 fixed the README's \"1–2+ GB\" caveat but missed web-ui.md. Align it\nwith the measured, bounded numbers (~150 MiB peak for a ~480 MiB-of-data\ncapture).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(diagnose): normalize count to always be ≥1 and clarify docs\n\nAddress PR review feedback:\n- pod.config-error catalog row now lists CreateContainerError alongside\n  CreateContainerConfigError (the rule fires for both).\n- count is now always serialized (drop omitempty) and normalized to ≥1 in\n  the engine, so -o json / CI consumers get a stable field. Docs updated to\n  match, and a test asserts singleton findings report count==1.\n- Document that `at` is only present when --at is passed (it is omitempty).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: correct web UI memory wording to match the benchmark\n\nThe memory benchmark logs a post-GC, steady-state retained footprint, not\nan instantaneous peak. Calling ~150 MiB a \"peak runtime footprint\" was\nmisleading — that number was the ~160 MiB cache ceiling, not a measurement.\nTestLargeCaptureMemory on a ~470 MiB / 48k-record capture retains ~20 MiB\npost-GC. Align README and docs/web-ui.md with what is actually measured.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
