          "distinct": true,
          "id": "247c3031d6d7716e7765258460f2259af9332c54",
          "message": "feat(replay): phase 2 — resourceVersion coherence, poll-only support, reconnect (#121) (#143)\n\n* feat(replay): phase 2 — resourceVersion coherence + poll-only support (#121)\n\nMake replay reliable for real Kubernetes informers and for captures taken\nwithout watch: true.\n\nresourceVersion coherence (the hard core):\n- A single time-sorted event timeline per watch path assigns every object a\n  monotonic RV (rv = base+index; rvAsOf(T) = base+count(t<=T)). Base 1 keeps\n  the window-start/empty RV non-zero. Because rv is a strict sequence (not a raw\n  timestamp), events sharing a timestamp — common for poll-only diffs — still\n  get distinct, ordered RVs.\n- LIST returns metadata.resourceVersion = rvAsOf(clock) (overridden in replay\n  mode); each streamed watch event object is stamped with its own rv; BOOKMARKs\n  carry rvAsOf of their list-as-of time.\n- WATCH honors resourceVersion: absent/\"0\" lists-then-streams; X>0 resumes with\n  no initial burst, streaming only rv > X. A reconnecting client resumes from\n  its last RV with no dropped/duplicated events.\n\nReconnect / relist:\n- A bogus or below-window resourceVersion returns 410 Gone (reason Expired) so\n  informers relist cleanly.\n\nPoll-only captures:\n- When a path has no watch index, the timeline is synthesized by diffing\n  consecutive snapshots (reusing internal/transitions); inferred events carry\n  their body inline. The CLI note and docs now describe inference instead of\n  \"nothing streams\".\n\nTimelines are memoized per path on the handler so LIST/WATCH don't rebuild them\n(important for poll-only, which diffs every snapshot).\n\nTests: RV monotonicity, LIST RV tracking the clock, resume-from-RV, reconnect\nwithout duplicates, 410 on stale/bogus RV, and a poll-only end-to-end stream.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(replay): address review — RV doc, timeline key, lazy list RV\n\n- Correct the RV-scheme doc comment to reflect replayRVBase: window-start RV is\n  1 and the first event's RV is 2 (base + index + 1).\n- Normalize the timeline cache key (trim trailing \"/\") so a LIST on \".../pods/\"\n  and a WATCH on \".../pods\" share one timeline (coherent RVs, warm cache).\n- Make rewriteListResourceVersion call an rvFn only after confirming the body is\n  a list, so single-object/discovery/Table responses don't build a (possibly\n  expensive, poll-only) timeline.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(replay): treat any zero-valued resourceVersion as unset\n\nParse resourceVersion before branching so \"0\", \"00\", etc. all map to the\nlist+stream (unset) path instead of falling into resume and returning 410. Added\na test covering \"0\" and \"00\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(replay): stamp list-burst RVs; build timeline without holding the lock\n\n- Stamp initial and relist ADDED-burst items with the list's coherent rv\n  (rvAsOf of the list-as-of time) instead of forwarding the captured object RV,\n  so a client resuming from an observed object RV aligns with the event stream.\n- timelineFor now builds the (possibly expensive, poll-only) timeline without\n  holding the mutex, so concurrent requests for other paths aren't blocked;\n  the first stored result wins if two goroutines race.\n\nAdded a test asserting burst items carry the coherent RV.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(replay): validate RV before building timeline; precise query handling\n\n- streamReplayWatch parses/validates resourceVersion first, so a malformed or\n  negative RV returns 410 without building the (poll-only-expensive) timeline;\n  the window check still runs after the timeline is built.\n- snapshotPaths skips only the \"?as=Table\" sentinel rather than every query key\n  (the capture engine merges pages into the bare list record; other query keys\n  never match the resource suffix anyway).\n- InferPollTransitions strips any query before parseAPIPath so resource metadata\n  stays correct even if a record is keyed with query params.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(replay): clarify timelineFor concurrent-build behavior\n\nThe comment overstated the guarantee. On a cold cache, several concurrent\ncallers for the same path may each build the timeline; the first stored result\nwins and the rest are discarded. Note singleflight as a future option.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(replay): 410 on too-large/unknown resourceVersion\n\nA numerically valid but too-large RV (e.g. a raw etcd RV pasted from the original\ncapture) was treated as a resume point and streamed nothing. Now return 410 Gone\nwhen the requested RV exceeds the maximum replay RV (replayRVBase + len(timeline))\nso the client relists, matching Kubernetes \"too old/unknown resourceVersion\"\nsemantics. Extended the stale-RV test with a too-large case.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(replay): validate resource path on resume watches (404)\n\nA resume watch (?resourceVersion=X) skipped resolveWatchList, so a watch on an\nunresolvable path returned 200 and streamed nothing. Always resolve the list for\nexistence/404 validation (response-cached); resume mode simply doesn't emit the\ninitial burst. Keeps resume and list+stream 404/500 semantics identical.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
