          "distinct": true,
          "id": "1215068c5b8549bf85e8ccfbde1e19ca4d12a366",
          "message": "feat(replay): phase 3 — dashboard transport controls (VCR) (#122) (#144)\n\n* feat(replay): phase 3 — dashboard transport controls (VCR)\n\nWire the v2 dashboard to a shared replay clock so it becomes a transport/VCR,\nand let both entry points share one clock:\n\n- `kshrk ui --speed/--from/--to/--loop/--start-paused` runs the dashboard in\n  replay mode (mock server + UI share the clock, so kubectl and the UI stay in\n  lockstep).\n- `kshrk replay --ui [--ui-port]` also starts the dashboard, sharing its clock.\n\nServer/UI:\n- ui.OpenOptions + v2.Handler carry an optional *server.ReplayClock; resolveAt\n  follows the clock when no explicit ?at= is given (explicit ?at= still wins).\n- New same-origin control API /v2/api/replay (GET status; POST play/pause/\n  speed/seek), backed by the clock. server.ParseSpeed is exported for it.\n\nFront-end (app.js/app.css):\n- Header transport bar (play/pause, step, 0.5x/1x/2x/3x speed, live event\n  count) shown only in replay mode. The scrubber seeks the clock; a poll loop\n  updates the thumb live and re-renders the current view as the clock crosses\n  each snapshot (throttled). Pause-on-error if a view fails mid-playback.\n\nTests: v2 replay control endpoint (status/pause/play/speed/seek + error paths)\nand resolveAt clock-follow. Docs: Replay (VCR) section in web-ui.md and the\n--ui flags / dashboard-transport note in usage.md.\n\nCloses #122.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(replay-ui): enforce control methods, safer resolveAt + pause-on-error\n\nAddress review feedback:\n- /v2/api/replay now enforces HTTP methods (GET for status, POST for\n  pause/play/speed/seek) with a 405 + Allow header, so state changes can't be\n  triggered by a GET/link navigation.\n- resolveAt: a present-but-unparseable ?at= falls back to h.At (previous\n  behavior) rather than silently following the live clock; the clock is used\n  only when ?at= is absent. Test covers the invalid-?at case.\n- Pause-on-error is now async-safe: render() (which returns a Promise) is\n  wrapped so both sync throws and async rejections pause playback, and getJSON\n  pauses replay when a data load fails mid-playback (view catch blocks otherwise\n  swallow the error into a panel).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(replay-ui): 404 control actions when replay off; safe control JSON parse\n\n- serveReplay: when not in replay mode, only GET status returns 200\n  {enabled:false}; any control action returns 404 so a non-UI client doesn't\n  see a mutating call succeed as a silent no-op. Test covers POST-when-off.\n- replayControl (JS): best-effort JSON parse + res.ok check (mirroring getJSON)\n  so a non-JSON error body doesn't mask the real HTTP status in the toast.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(replay-ui): floor snapshot index + reflect non-preset speed\n\n- Use the floor snapshot index (latest snapshot at/before the clock) instead of\n  the nearest, so the auto-follow view re-renders exactly when the clock crosses\n  a snapshot rather than at the midpoint between two. Renamed the helper to\n  replaySnapshotIndex and updated all call sites.\n- The speed selector now includes the current speed even when it isn't one of\n  the presets (e.g. a server started with --speed 5x), so it reflects real state\n  instead of snapping to the first option.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(replay-ui): reject --at combined with replay flags\n\n--at pins a single instant, which the replay clock overrides, so passing it with\nany replay flag was silently ignored. `kshrk ui` now errors with a message\npointing to --from/--to. Added a cmd test.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(replay-ui): reject cross-origin control POSTs; guard overlapping polls\n\n- /v2/api/replay mutations (pause/play/speed/seek) now reject a request whose\n  Origin header is present and cross-origin (403), so an unrelated web page can't\n  POST to the local dashboard and move the clock. Non-browser clients (curl,\n  which omit Origin) are still allowed. Test covers cross- vs same-origin.\n- pollReplay uses an in-flight guard so a slow response can't let overlapping\n  polls apply out-of-order statuses (thumb jumping backward / extra renders).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(replay-ui): keep speed dropdown open; presets 0.25x/0.5x/1x/2x\n\nThe transport bar was fully rebuilt on every 700ms poll (box.innerHTML = ''),\nwhich recreated the <select> and closed the native speed dropdown before a user\ncould pick an option. Build the transport elements once and update them in place\n(play/pause label, speed options only when the set changes, events counter,\nended badge); skip clobbering the select's value while it's focused. Also change\nthe presets to 0.25x / 0.5x / 1x / 2x (the current speed is still added if it\nisn't a preset).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
