          "distinct": true,
          "id": "e4889054cf57c9fec1ec2b6fcd60a46ad74744f7",
          "message": "fix(ci): conformance PR comment silently broken (gh --slurp + --jq) (#147)\n\n* fix(ci): conformance PR comment — gh rejects --slurp with --jq\n\nThe \"Comment results on PR\" step used `gh api --paginate --slurp --jq ...`,\nbut gh forbids --slurp together with --jq/--template, so the step errored\n(\"the --slurp option is not supported with --jq or --template\") and, being\ncontinue-on-error, failed silently — no comment was ever posted.\n\nDrop --slurp: let --paginate + --jq emit the id of each matching comment\nacross all pages (one per line) and take the first with `head -n1`. This is\ndeterministic and keeps the multi-page safety the --slurp change was after.\n\nVerified against a real paginated PR thread: the old form errors as reported;\nthe new form returns the single correct conformance-report comment id.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci(conformance): surface comment failures as a ::warning:: annotation\n\nThe results-comment step is continue-on-error (so a comment hiccup can't fail\nthe conformance gate), which previously let a real breakage pass silently.\nNow the step traps any gh failure (lookup/update/create) and emits a\n::warning:: annotation instead of failing quietly, so future breakage is\nvisible in the run without gating the check.\n\nAlso capture the id list into a variable rather than piping gh into `head`,\nso gh's exit status is actually checked and a closed pipe can't SIGPIPE gh\ninto a spurious failure.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-09T12:11:24-04:00",
