          "distinct": true,
          "id": "72f086166c256a67222203fbca163650c0e34b84",
          "message": "feat(server): accept protobuf request bodies for writable-overlay writes (#151)\n\n* feat(server): decode protobuf request bodies for writable-overlay writes\n\nThe writable overlay only accepted JSON, but kubectl/client-go/controllers\ndefault to Content-Type: application/vnd.kubernetes.protobuf for built-in\ntypes, so their writes were rejected with 400 \"request body must be a JSON\nobject\" — making the overlay unusable with standard tooling.\n\nNormalize the request body to JSON at the write ingress: when the Content-Type\nis application/vnd.kubernetes.protobuf, decode the k8s\\x00-framed body into a\ntyped object via the built-in client-go scheme and re-encode it as JSON, then\nfeed the existing JSON create/replace path. Everything downstream (overlay\nstore, LIST merge, watch events) stays JSON. JSON writes are unchanged; a\nmalformed protobuf body is a clean 400. No new dependencies (k8s.io/api,\napimachinery, client-go already required).\n\nVerified: `kubectl create namespace` (default protobuf) now succeeds against\n`kshrk replay --writable`, and the CNCF conformance BeforeEach advances past\nnamespace creation (it then blocks on live-cluster-only default-ServiceAccount\nprovisioning, which is out of scope for a replay).\n\nCloses #148\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(server): fail on response-body read error in protobuf test helper\n\nHandle the io.ReadAll error in doReqBytes rather than discarding it, so a\ntransport-level failure surfaces as a clear test failure instead of a\nconfusing empty body.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(server): cover protobuf replace (PUT), not just create\n\nreadObjectBody serves both create and replace; add a protobuf PUT round-trip\n(and a malformed-body 400) for the overlayReplace path.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
