          "distinct": true,
          "id": "cabe593e6cd8b729e8bbf068a566c0f12cdb6eed",
          "message": "feat(server): namespace defaults (SA + kube-root-ca) + WatchList support for the writable overlay (#154)\n\n* feat(server): synthesize default ServiceAccount on namespace create\n\nIn the writable overlay, creating a namespace now also synthesizes the\n`default` ServiceAccount that a real cluster's controller would auto-create —\nthe overlay has no controllers, so clients (and the e2e framework) that wait\nfor it would otherwise hang. Modern Kubernetes (1.24+) provisions no token\nSecret for the default SA, so a bare SA object suffices; it's stored in the\noverlay so it's gettable, listable, and watchable in the new namespace.\n\nVerified: `kubectl create namespace X` then `kubectl get sa default -n X`\nreturns the SA (single-GET, list, and watch all surface it).\n\nPart of #152. NOTE: this alone does not yet get the CNCF conformance\nBeforeEach past its ServiceAccount wait — that wait uses a client-go\nWatchList informer (sendInitialEvents=true) which requires an\n`k8s.io/initial-events-end: \"true\"` annotated BOOKMARK the mock does not emit\nyet. Filed separately.\n\nRefs #152\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(server): WatchList support + kube-root-ca.crt so informers/BeforeEach clear\n\nBuilds on the default-SA synthesis to make the writable overlay usable by\nclient-go informers and the CNCF conformance framework's per-test BeforeEach:\n\n- Watch initial burst now merges overlay writes (resolveWatchList applies the\n  overlay like the LIST path). Previously a WatchList informer's watch-only\n  initial events never observed overlay-created objects (e.g. the synthesized\n  default ServiceAccount), so it never synced.\n- Support the WatchList protocol (client-go 1.32+, sendInitialEvents=true):\n  terminate the initial burst with a BOOKMARK carrying the\n  k8s.io/initial-events-end annotation. Both the replay and plain watch paths.\n- Synthesize the kube-root-ca.crt ConfigMap alongside the default SA on\n  namespace create (another object a real cluster's controller provisions and\n  the framework waits for). Generalized into ensureNamespaceDefaults /\n  synthesizeOverlayObject.\n\nVerified end-to-end: against `kshrk replay --writable`, the conformance\nBeforeEach now fully clears (default SA + kube-root-ca + informer sync all\npass) and specs reach their actual test bodies — they then fail on real\ndiscovery-content / namespace-GC gaps, which are separate/deeper (out of scope\nhere). `go test -race ./internal/server/`, vet, gofmt all clean.\n\nCloses #152\nCloses #153\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
