          "distinct": true,
          "id": "26ae9c6f78bafeadaeb18e8deae1a43352493676",
          "message": "feat(replay-overlay): cascade namespace deletion to its contents (#157)\n\n* feat(replay-overlay): cascade namespace deletion to its contents\n\nDeleting a namespace in the writable overlay left its objects behind (no\nnamespace/GC controller runs against the overlay) — e.g. a deployment created in\na deleted namespace still showed in `kubectl get deploy -A`. Synthesize the\ncascade in the overlay:\n\n- On namespace delete, eager-tombstone every overlay object in that namespace\n  (cascadeDeleteNamespace) so overlay-created contents don't linger or resurrect.\n- Lazy read filter for the rest: a single-object GET in a deleted namespace 404s,\n  and LIST responses (namespaced and cluster-wide/-A) drop items whose namespace\n  was deleted — covering captured objects too, without enumerating the capture.\n- Reject create/update into a deleted namespace (404), matching \"namespace gone\".\n- Re-creating the namespace un-deletes it (its old contents stay tombstoned).\n\nTests: overlay deployment disappears from -A/namespaced/GET after ns delete;\ncreate-into-deleted-ns 404s; captured objects in a deleted namespace are hidden.\n\nPart of #123. Stacked on #149 (parseWritePath fix needed to route the namespace\nDELETE).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(replay-overlay): 404 all writes into a deleted namespace; fix comments\n\nAddress Copilot review on #157:\n- overlay.go: fix stale doc symbol name (coreNamespacesGVR -> isCoreNamespace).\n- writes.go: drop the DELETE exemption in the namespace-deleted guard. A\n  deleted namespace takes its contents with it, so a DELETE of a still-captured\n  object in it should 404 too (currentObject reads the store regardless), not\n  return 200. Reword the comment to match.\n- writes_test.go: assert DELETE of an object in a deleted namespace 404s.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-09T23:09:19-04:00",
          "tree_id": "d8b408e460d9fddb2ceb324ceff6dac58093098a",
