          "distinct": true,
          "id": "2ea7ea181a315b53ee5040e86ca5fd9753d2f5c7",
          "message": "feat(replay-overlay): strategic-merge patch for built-in types (#161)\n\n* feat(replay-overlay): strategic-merge patch for built-in types\n\nPhase-4 PR 3 of the writable overlay (#123). Until now\napplication/strategic-merge-patch+json fell back to a plain JSON merge patch,\nwhich replaces keyed lists wholesale — e.g. patching one container by name would\ndrop the others.\n\nRoute strategic-merge patches through apimachinery's strategicpatch using the\nobject's registered built-in type (scheme.Scheme.New on its GVK), so keyed lists\n(containers by name, etc.) merge element-wise, matching the kube-apiserver.\nStrategic merge is only defined for built-in types — the apiserver has no strategy\nmetadata for custom resources — so an object whose GVK isn't in the scheme falls\nback to a JSON merge patch. No new module dependencies: client-go's scheme and\nthe typed API are already in the graph.\n\nTests: TestOverlay_StrategicMergePatch (keyed list merged element-wise) and\nTestOverlay_MergePatchReplacesList (the contrasting merge-patch behavior).\n\nNote: the /status subresource endpoint already isolates status correctly\n(replaceField); spec/status isolation on the *main* endpoint needs subresource\nregistration data the mock doesn't track and is left as a follow-up.\n\nPart of #123.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(replay-overlay): resolve strategic-merge GVK from the path, not the body\n\nAddress Copilot review on #161: strategicMergePatch derived the target type from\nthe stored object's apiVersion/kind, but a replayed object reconstructed from a\ncaptured LIST has no TypeMeta (the apiserver strips it from list items), so a\nstrategic patch of such an object silently degraded to a JSON merge — dropping\nsibling list elements, the exact bug this PR fixes.\n\nDerive the GVK from the request path's group/version/resource (via resourceToKind)\ninstead; the path is always authoritative for the resource being patched. Adds\nTestOverlay_StrategicMergePatch_CapturedNoTypeMeta covering a TypeMeta-less\ncaptured object.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(replay-overlay): resolve strategic-merge Kind from the scheme, not a heuristic\n\nAddress Copilot review on #161: resourceToKind is a name-capitalization heuristic\nthat mis-cases some built-in Kinds (e.g. endpointslices → \"Endpointslice\" instead\nof \"EndpointSlice\"), so scheme.New would fail and strategic merge would silently\ndegrade to a JSON merge for those types.\n\nResolve the Kind by inverting the apiserver's own kind→resource convention\n(meta.UnsafeGuessKindToResource) over the scheme's KnownTypes for the group/\nversion — exact for every registered built-in type. Custom resources (no match)\nstill fall back to a JSON merge patch.\n\nAdds TestKindForResource covering pods/configmaps/deployments, the EndpointSlice\nmis-casing case, networkpolicies, and a custom resource (ok=false).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
