          "distinct": true,
          "id": "fa9eab80183f21add98aada0371dbfcdf6d7abcd",
          "message": "feat(replay): KWOK convenience — --with-kwok, --schedule-pods, eager node synthesis (#167)\n\n* feat(replay): KWOK convenience — --with-kwok, --schedule-pods, eager node synth\n\nThe three optional follow-ups from #160:\n\n- --with-kwok: implies --writable, then runs a detected `kwok` binary against the\n  server (--manage-all-nodes + the bundled stages embedded from\n  examples/kwok-stages.yaml) and stops it on exit. Clear install hint when the\n  kwok binary isn't on PATH. The whole closed loop in one process.\n- --schedule-pods (default true): opt out of the pod-scheduling shim via\n  ReplayOptions.DisableScheduling (zero value keeps the shim on, so ui.go's\n  writable mode is unchanged).\n- Eager node synthesis: serve() synthesizes the fake node at startup when the\n  capture has none, so `kubectl get nodes` (and KWOK) sees it before any Pod.\n\nStages are embedded in the module-root package (go:embed can't reach a sibling\ndir from cmd/) and injected into cmd via KwokStages.\n\nTests: TestSchedule_EagerNodeSynthesis, TestStartKwok_NotInstalled,\nTestKwokStagesEmbedded. Closes the optional items from #160.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(replay): check temp stages-file Close in startKwok\n\nAddress Copilot review on #167: startKwok ignored the error from closing the temp\nstages file. Close flushes the write, so a silent failure could leave the file\nincomplete and surface later as a confusing kwok parse error. Check it and clean\nup on failure.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(replay): reject --with-kwok with --schedule-pods=false\n\nAddress Copilot review on #167: --with-kwok only forced --writable but still\nallowed --schedule-pods=false. That combination is self-defeating — KWOK only\nadvances pods bound to a node, so with the scheduling shim off pods stay\nunscheduled and the advertised Pending→Running loop never fires. Reject it with a\nclear error (validateKwokFlags) instead of failing silently.\n\nAdds TestValidateKwokFlags.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(replay): re-synthesize the scheduling node after an overlay reset\n\nAddress Copilot review on #167: eager node synthesis ran only once at startup,\nbut syncEpoch clears the overlay on a loop wrap (and manual reset clears it too),\ndropping the synthetic kwok-node-0. For a nodeless capture that left KWOK's node\nPATCHes 404ing and `kubectl get nodes` empty until a later write re-synthesized.\n\noverlay.syncEpoch now reports whether it reset; a new handler-level h.syncEpoch()\n(used by all read/write/watch entry points) re-runs ensureSchedulableNode on\nreset, and the manual reset-overlay control does the same. Idempotent via\nstoreIfAbsent.\n\nAdds TestSchedule_ReensuresNodeAfterLoopReset.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
