          "distinct": true,
          "id": "3993457182befbf9056f1d6b4a7ca72602278837",
          "message": "feat(server): compute kubectl Table output for overlay & uncaptured objects (#168)\n\n* feat(server): compute kubectl Table output for overlay & uncaptured objects\n\n`kubectl get <resource>` / `-o wide` against the mock served the captured\nserver-side Table verbatim when present (faithful), but fell back to a generic\nNAME/(NAMESPACE)/AGE table otherwise. That generic fallback fired for kinds and\ncaptures lacking a stored Table, and — because the captured-Table fast paths are\nbypassed in writable mode — for every object in a writable overlay, including\nobjects created after capture. So `kubectl get` on overlay-created or\nnever-captured resources didn't match a live cluster.\n\nAdd internal/server/table.go: a Table renderer plus a per-GVK printer registry.\nrenderResourceTable computes columnDefinitions + per-object cells for an\narbitrary set of objects, choosing columns by precedence:\n\n  1. a built-in per-kind printer for ~19 core/native kinds (Node, Pod, the\n     workloads, Service, Endpoints, Ingress, ConfigMap, Secret, PVC, PV,\n     Namespace, ServiceAccount, Event) — columns mirror upstream kubectl,\n     including `-o wide` columns via per-column priority;\n  2. a CRD printer built from the captured CRD's additionalPrinterColumns\n     (JSONPath cells);\n  3. the captured columnDefinitions for the kind + metadata-only cells;\n  4. the generic buildTable.\n\nAGE is emitted as a pre-computed relative string (\"5m49s\", \"2d\") against the\nreplay clock, and column order matches upstream (e.g. nodes: NAME STATUS ROLES\nAGE VERSION). Single-object GET paths (`kubectl get <resource> <name>`) resolve\nto the same printer as the list path.\n\nWire into serveResource: read-only fully-captured requests still serve the\ncaptured Table verbatim; writable mode / no-stored-Table / single overlay\nobjects now render through renderResourceTable.\n\nCloses #166\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(server): CronJob containers, RC/Service selector, single-object fallbacks\n\nAddress review feedback on the Table renderer:\n\n- containersCol/imagesCol now resolve the CronJob pod template via the nested\n  spec.jobTemplate (was always empty for CronJob `-o wide`).\n- selectorCol handles the plain-map selector used by ReplicationController and\n  Service (spec.selector), not just apps/v1 spec.selector.matchLabels.\n- renderResourceTable returns ok=false when a single-object body fails to decode\n  (was emitting an empty rows Table).\n- capturedColumns lookup uses the resolved list path so single-object GETs reuse\n  the list's stored columnDefinitions.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(server): jobStatus Suspended state + captured Age column type\n\nAddress second-round review feedback:\n\n- jobStatus dropped the dead active-count branch (both arms returned \"Running\")\n  and now returns \"Suspended\" for a suspended Job, matching kubectl's STATUS\n  column (Complete/Failed condition → Suspended → Running).\n- capturedColumns marks the Age column type \"string\" when reusing captured\n  columnDefinitions, since its cell is emitted as a relative-age string (\"5m\",\n  \"2d\") — the captured type was often \"date\", which mismatched the value.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* perf(server): consistent generic-table AGE + memoize CRD columns\n\nAddress third-round review feedback:\n\n- The last-resort generic table now renders through renderTableFromColumns\n  (NAME / NAMESPACE / AGE) so AGE is a relative string like the computed tiers,\n  instead of the raw RFC3339 timestamp the removed buildTable emitted. buildTable\n  is deleted (it was the only remaining raw-timestamp path).\n- crdPrinterColumns memoizes resolved columns per group/version/resource\n  (handler.crdColsCache). CaptureStore.ReconstructAt caches by exact clock time,\n  so an advancing replay clock previously reconstructed+parsed the entire CRD\n  list on every custom-resource render; additionalPrinterColumns are effectively\n  static, so resolving once (negatives included) removes the per-request O(N_CRDs)\n  work. A CRD changed mid-replay isn't reflected — acceptable for a mock.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(server): fix stale buildTable comment + fractional-second age test\n\nFourth-round review follow-up:\n\n- Update the serveResource comment that still referenced the removed\n  \"generic buildTable\"; the last-resort fallback is now a computed generic\n  NAME/(NAMESPACE)/AGE table.\n- Add a regression test proving humanAge handles RFC3339Nano\n  (fractional-second) creationTimestamps — Go's time.Parse(time.RFC3339, …)\n  accepts a fractional-second field on input, so no code change is needed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(server): purge remaining stale buildTable references\n\nUpdate the three doc comments that still named the removed buildTable; the\nlast-resort tier is a computed generic NAME/(NAMESPACE)/AGE table. No behavior\nchange.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(server): computed-table AGE uses capture end time in open mode\n\nIn plain `open` mode without `--at`, the handler passes the zero time (which the\nstore reads as \"latest\") into renderResourceTable. humanAge then fell back to\nnow=creationTimestamp and emitted \"0s\" for every object in a computed Table\n(kinds/captures without a stored Table).\n\nResolve an effective \"now\": when at is zero, use the capture's end time\n(store.Metadata.CapturedUntil), so AGE reflects the captured cluster's clock.\nat is still used unchanged for the store lookups, where zero means \"latest\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(server): captured-column fallback cells emit null, not empty string\n\nFor captured columns that can't be recomputed for a new object, the fallback\ncell now returns JSON null instead of \"\". null is valid for any declared column\ntype (integer/date/etc.); an empty string mistypes non-string columns.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(server): correct renderTableFromColumns comment (no raw bytes)\n\nThe function receives decoded object maps and builds each row's\nPartialObjectMetadata from the decoded metadata; it has no raw object bytes.\nComment-only change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(server): pod READY denominator uses spec.containers\n\npodReady used len(status.containerStatuses) as the total, so a just-created or\nPending pod with no statuses yet rendered \"0/0\". Use the spec container count\nlike kubectl (falling back to containerStatuses when spec.containers is absent),\nso it reads e.g. \"0/1\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
