          "distinct": true,
          "id": "864a141ef31ce0f06e75fdd714442d39171c6a97",
          "message": "fix(replay): don't synthesize kwok-node-0 for captures that have nodes (#173)\n\nEager node synthesis under --writable decided \"the capture has no nodes\" by\nchecking knownNodeNames() at the replay clock's current instant, which at startup\nis the window start `from` (≈ metadata.CapturedAt, an approximation). A capture's\nfirst /api/v1/nodes snapshot commonly lands a few seconds after `from`, so the\ncheck saw no nodes and injected a synthetic kwok-node-0 even for captures that\nclearly contain nodes — most visible in `kshrk ui --writable` (which sits at\n`from`, especially --start-paused).\n\nEvaluate node presence at the window END (clock.Window()) instead, so a node\nwhose first snapshot post-dates `from` still counts. knownNodeNames is refactored\ninto knownNodeNamesAt(at); the scheduling shim keeps using the clock instant.\nNodeless captures still synthesize kwok-node-0 (intended KWOK behavior), and the\nlazy on-first-pod synthesis path is unchanged.\n\nCloses #172\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-14T12:02:17-04:00",
          "tree_id": "2c5be7deaf5ce4fdcee6877c6c331becd024defa",
