          "distinct": true,
          "id": "135cfe8591053c9c56d450f7106f7c3162938d47",
          "message": "fix(capture,replay): stop --with-kwok's kwok from racing the replay clock (#183)\n\n* fix(server): known-but-uncaptured kinds behave like empty live collections\n\nA kind present in a captured discovery document but with zero captured\nobjects was indistinguishable from a genuinely unknown/misconfigured kind:\nresourceInfo was only ever derived from index paths (buildResourceInfo) and\nenrichResourceInfoFromDiscovery only enriched existing entries, so a\nnever-captured resource type never got a ResourceInfo entry at all — even\nthough its discovery document listed it. That meant the mock server's own\ndiscovery response for that group/version omitted it too, and LIST/GET\nbehaved as if the kind didn't exist.\n\n- enrichResourceInfoFromDiscovery now creates a new entry (mergeResourceInfo)\n  for a resource the discovery document lists but the index doesn't, instead\n  of skipping it. resourceInfo access is now mutex-guarded (this background\n  pass now inserts new map keys, not just mutates existing entries' fields —\n  unlike a field mutation, a concurrent map insert during Resources()'s range\n  is unsafe).\n- Added CaptureStore.isKnownResource and a discoveryEnrichmentDone WaitGroup\n  so tests can deterministically wait for the background enrichment pass\n  instead of racing it (production code still doesn't wait, as documented).\n- serveResource's LIST 404-fallback now only sets the \"not found in capture\"\n  Warning header for a genuinely unknown resource; a known one gets a plain\n  empty 200, matching a real cluster's empty live collection.\n- serveResource's item-GET 404 now returns a standard Kubernetes NotFound\n  Status (reason: NotFound, proper message/details via the new\n  notFoundStatus helper) instead of a k8shark-specific message, so\n  apierrors.IsNotFound() recognizes it — matching the real apiserver's\n  create → delete → confirm-gone-with-IsNotFound pattern.\n\nCloses #177\n\n* fix(server): correct three edge cases in the #177 known-kind fix\n\nCopilot review turned up three real gaps:\n\n- mergeResourceInfo only applied discovery's namespaced field when creating a\n  new entry; enriching an existing (index-derived) entry left it unchanged.\n  A capture with only a cluster-wide list (no namespaces: in config) for a\n  namespaced resource would report it as cluster-scoped in the regenerated\n  discovery document. Discovery's namespaced field is now authoritative on\n  every merge, not just creation.\n- Resources() returned the original *ResourceInfo pointers stored in the map\n  after releasing the RWMutex, so a caller reading fields after the call\n  returns could race with mergeResourceInfo mutating the same struct from the\n  background discovery-enrichment goroutine. Now returns value-copy\n  snapshots taken under the lock.\n- The item-GET NotFound Status fix applied to any well-formed item path,\n  even for a genuinely unknown resource (wrong group/resource entirely) —\n  presenting a capture-config problem as \"the object is just missing\".\n  Gated behind isKnownResource, matching the LIST-warning fix's philosophy;\n  an unknown resource keeps the k8shark-specific message.\n\n* fix(server): deep-copy ShortNames in Resources() to fully decouple snapshots\n\nA struct copy alone still shares ResourceInfo.ShortNames' backing array with\nthe stored entry, so a caller mutating a returned ShortNames slice would\ncorrupt internal state without holding resourceInfoMu — reintroducing the\nunsafe-concurrent-access class Resources() was just changed to avoid. Copy\nShortNames into a fresh backing array too.\n\n* fix(server): use discovery's Kind for the empty-LIST fallback, not the heuristic\n\nresourceToKind's map-plus-depluralization heuristic guesses wrong for\nresources whose Kind doesn't follow simple depluralization (e.g.\n\"endpointslices\" -> \"Endpointslice\" instead of the real \"EndpointSlice\") and\nfor most CRDs. Added CaptureStore.resourceKind, which returns the\nauthoritative Kind from captured discovery/index metadata when the resource\nis known, falling back to the heuristic only when it's genuinely unknown. A\nclient deserializing the empty-list response by GVK would otherwise break.\n\n* fix(capture,replay): stop --with-kwok's kwok from racing the replay clock\n\nCaptureMetadata.CapturedAt was backdated as `finish - configured duration`,\nwhich silently absorbed any preflight/version-check/discovery time spent\nbefore the first poll actually fired. Since a replay session defaults its\nwindow start to CapturedAt, an underestimated CapturedAt could land before a\nresource's first captured snapshot — so a client querying right at replay\nstart (most notably `replay --with-kwok`'s auto-launched kwok subprocess\npolling /api/v1/nodes on its very first LIST) could see a spurious \"not found\nin capture\" for a resource that genuinely was captured. Because kwok's node\ninformer only LISTs once at startup, losing that race left its node cache\nempty for the whole session, so pods it managed never reached Running.\n\nRecord CapturedAt right before the poll/watch goroutines launch instead of\nback-computing it, and add a readiness wait before starting the auto-launched\nkwok subprocess as a second line of defense against the residual (much\nsmaller) scheduling/network jitter.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(replay): pin the mock server's cert instead of skipping TLS verification\n\nCodeQL flagged waitForNodesReady's InsecureSkipVerify: true. Since it's an\nin-process client hitting an HTTPS listener we just spawned ourselves, the\nreal self-signed certificate is available — pin it (via a new\nServer.CertPEM() accessor) instead of disabling verification.\n\nAlso bound each readiness request's timeout to the remaining overall budget\n(previously a fixed 2s per-request timeout, checked only after the request\nreturned, could let one slow/hung response push the wait well past the\nintended overall timeout), per Copilot review feedback.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(server): return a defensive copy from Server.CertPEM()\n\nReturning the internal slice directly let a caller mutate it and corrupt\nsubsequent CertPEM() callers' view of the cert.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
