          "distinct": true,
          "id": "01c4ad26eb84d10f2aa71581fa7152b69f581f5d",
          "message": "fix(server,ui): default paused replay clock to window end, not start (#188)\n\n* fix(server,ui): default paused replay clock to window end, not start\n\nkshrk ui --writable (and any other replay-flag combo) starts paused per\n#179, but pinned the clock to the window start — a capture's opening\nmoments are typically sparse since informers are still completing their\ninitial LIST, so `kubectl get pods -A` etc. showed near-empty results\nuntil the user opened the dashboard and pressed Play. Starting the\npaused position at the window end shows the most complete captured\nstate by default; explicit auto-play still starts at the window start\nand plays forward as before.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(server): scope the window-end pause default to the Web UI only\n\nCopilot review on #188 caught a real regression: NewReplayClock's default\npaused-position change applied to every StartPaused caller, including\nheadless `kshrk replay --start-paused`, which documents \"press Enter to\nbegin playback\" from the window start — with a clock anchored at `to`,\nResume() would immediately re-clamp to `to` and the replay would never\nadvance.\n\nRevert NewReplayClock to always start at `from`. Add a ReplayOptions.\nPauseAtWindowEnd flag (set only by cmd/ui.go) and a new\nReplayClock.ParkAtWindowEnd(), which positions a paused clock at the\nwindow end for preview without marking the replay as having ended, and\nwithout breaking Resume: it rewinds to `from` and plays forward normally\ninstead of re-reporting the end it was parked at. An explicit Seek still\nclears the preview state, since the user has now chosen a position.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(server): bump SeekGen on the parked-at-end Resume rewind\n\nAnother Copilot catch on #188: Resume()'s parkedAtEnd rewind moved\ncaptureAnchor from `to` back to `from` without bumping SeekGen. A watch\nstream that connected while parked at the end has already exhausted its\ntimeline and is blocked in waitForRestart, which only wakes on a SeekGen\nor epoch change — without the bump, it would idle for the rest of\nplayback despite the clock now actively advancing. Also corrected the\nparkedAtEnd doc comment, which inaccurately described a \"second Resume\"\nclearing the flag when it's cleared by the same call that rewinds.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(server): fix stale NewReplayClock comment pointing at Seek\n\nThird Copilot catch on #188: the comment (written before ParkAtWindowEnd\nexisted) told callers wanting a paused-elsewhere clock to just Seek()\nafter construction. That's wrong now — Seek(to) reports ended=true while\nparked and skips Resume's rewind-and-play behavior. Point at\nParkAtWindowEnd instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
