          "distinct": true,
          "id": "fa223dad06a40168f624f66b90fc4098c06c9e14",
          "message": "build(release): add k8shark@rc Homebrew channel; keep stable tap off prereleases (#189)\n\nThe GoReleaser brews entry had no skip_upload, so cutting a prerelease tag\n(e.g. v0.5.1-rc.1) overwrote the tap's k8shark.rb — making\n`brew install phenixblue/tap/k8shark` serve the RC to everyone.\n\n- Stable entry: skip_upload=auto so a prerelease tag no longer updates k8shark.rb\n  (the tap tracks the latest stable again).\n- New k8shark@rc entry: the inverse (skip_upload uploads only when .Prerelease is\n  non-empty), so `brew install phenixblue/tap/k8shark@rc` tracks the latest RC.\n\nBoth formulae install the same kshrk binary and therefore conflict — users pick a\nchannel. Docs updated with the @rc install and the go-install prerelease pin.\n\nNote: the tap's k8shark.rb is currently pinned to 0.5.1-rc.1; a companion change\nresets it to v0.4.0 (this config prevents recurrence on the next release).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-17T00:07:47-04:00",
          "tree_id": "0fe18793420988b747ecb35d3b92702879fd8d19",
