          "distinct": true,
          "id": "3561528131350bcef20922380e44a5782fa42e86",
          "message": "fix(server): writable overlay fidelity gaps found via the upstream conformance suite (#190)\n\n* fix(server): writable overlay fidelity gaps found via the upstream conformance suite\n\nDiscovered and fixed by actually running kube-controller-manager and the\nupstream [Conformance] apps/network suite against --writable\n--with-kwok --with-controller-manager, not just unit tests:\n\n- Server-Side Apply (Content-Type: application/apply-patch+yaml) now\n  creates an object on first apply instead of 404ing — matching the real\n  apiserver's create-or-update semantics. This is what `helm install\n  --create-namespace`, `kubectl apply --server-side`, and CRD/webhook\n  installers all rely on.\n- Deployment/StatefulSet/ReplicaSet default `.spec.replicas` to 1 when\n  omitted (some charts, e.g. istiod, rely on this apiserver default); a\n  nil value panics the deployment controller's NewRSNewReplicas.\n- StatefulSet/DaemonSet default `.spec.revisionHistoryLimit` to 10 when\n  omitted. Unlike Deployment's equivalent cleanup path (which nil-checks\n  first), these controllers' history-truncation code dereferences it\n  unconditionally — a nil value crashed the entire kube-controller-manager\n  process, silently killing all reconciliation for the rest of a run.\n- A `LoadBalancer` Service gets a synthesized external IP and ClusterIP.\n  kstatus (which Helm v4's `--wait` uses) specifically requires\n  `spec.clusterIP` non-empty for LoadBalancer Services — not the external\n  address — so a Service missing one hung `helm install --wait` forever.\n- Added `/scale` subresource support (GET/PUT/PATCH) for Deployment/\n  ReplicaSet/StatefulSet/ReplicationController.\n- Fixed the status subresource to protect only `.spec` (reset to current),\n  matching real per-type apiserver strategies — it previously protected\n  all of metadata too, silently dropping the\n  `deployment.kubernetes.io/revision` annotation the deployment controller\n  sets via `UpdateStatus` (a full-object PUT to `.../status`).\n- A watch resuming from `resourceVersion=X>0` now catches up on overlay\n  writes already committed between X and when the watch connects,\n  correctly replayed as ADDED or MODIFIED depending on whether the\n  identity existed as of X. This is the exact race client-go's\n  List-then-Watch pattern relies on a real apiserver's watch cache to\n  cover; our overlay's live pub-sub only reached watchers already\n  subscribed at write time, hanging any client watching for its own\n  just-created or just-updated object.\n- Write responses (create/replace/patch) now stamp apiVersion/kind like\n  reads and watch events already did. client-go's typed Update/\n  UpdateStatus calls round-trip an object whose TypeMeta the apiserver\n  strips on read, so the request body often omits it — but a real\n  apiserver's response is always fully typed, and a typed client-go\n  decoder fails on the response with \"Object 'Kind' is missing\"\n  otherwise.\n- Synthesized the version-less APIGroup discovery document\n  (/apis/<group>, distinct from /apis/<group>/<version>'s resource list)\n  — client-go's discovery client fetches this to enumerate a group's\n  versions before making a versioned request, and it 404'd even though\n  the versioned path worked fine, breaking any client (e.g. the\n  Ingress/IngressClass API conformance specs) that discovers a group\n  this way first.\n\nEach fix's regression test was verified to fail (hang or wrong output)\nbefore the fix and pass after, not just added alongside it. Full suite,\n`go vet`, `gofmt`, and `-race` all clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(server): address Copilot review findings on PR #190\n\n- serveAPIGroup/serveAPIGroupList: CaptureStore.Resources() iterates a\n  map, so the preferredVersion each returned was nondeterministic across\n  calls for any group with multiple captured versions. Sort by real\n  Kubernetes version priority (k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/version's\n  CompareKubeAwareVersionStrings — GA descending, then beta, then alpha)\n  instead, shared via a new sortedGroupVersions helper.\n- overlayScaleWrite: PATCH .../scale accepted\n  Content-Type: application/apply-patch+yaml (Server-Side Apply) per\n  supportedPatchType, but jsonMergeOrPatch had no YAML handling, so an\n  apply-patch request would 422 instead of scaling. Convert YAML to JSON\n  first, matching the main write path's applyPatch.\n- scaleObject: only decoded .spec.selector as a structured\n  metav1.LabelSelector, which silently succeeds (with a zero-value\n  result) against ReplicationController's plain map[string]string\n  selector — unknown JSON fields on a struct are ignored, not an error —\n  so RC Scale responses always had an empty status.selector. Try the map\n  shape first (a real LabelSelector's nested matchLabels/matchExpressions\n  can't decode into map[string]string, so it fails reliably) before\n  falling back to LabelSelector parsing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
