          "distinct": true,
          "id": "7acc9037ea0ba16b8854bcb02a07dfe717420cb9",
          "message": "fix(server): synthesize CRD Established status on create (#191)\n\n* fix(server): synthesize CRD Established status on create\n\nA real apiextensions-apiserver establishes a freshly created\nCustomResourceDefinition (status.conditions Established/NamesAccepted,\nacceptedNames, storedVersions) within moments of creation — this is\ninternal to kube-apiserver, not something --with-controller-manager's\ncurated kube-controller-manager set runs. Without it, kstatus (which\nHelm v4's --wait uses) reports every CRD \"InProgress: Install in\nprogress\" forever, hanging any CRD-heavy chart install — found by\nre-running a real `helm install istio-base` end to end after merging\n#190, which install several dozen CRDs and hung on exactly this.\n\nstoreNewObject now synthesizes this status for a newly created CRD,\nmatching the existing pattern for other controller-provided defaults\nthe overlay has no controller for (default ServiceAccount,\nkube-root-ca.crt, LoadBalancer/ClusterIP synthesis, etc.).\n\nVerified end-to-end: `helm install istio-base/istiod/istio-ingress\n--wait` all now succeed against a real kube-controller-manager +\nwritable overlay, where istio-base previously hung for the full\n--wait timeout on its ~20 CRDs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(deps): bump golang.org/x/text to v0.39.0 (GO-2026-5970)\n\ngovulncheck flagged an infinite-loop-on-invalid-input vulnerability in\nthe transitive dependency golang.org/x/text@v0.38.0, fixed in v0.39.0.\nUnrelated to this PR's actual change; bumping to unblock the \"vuln\" CI\ncheck.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(server): address Copilot review findings on PR #191\n\n- ensureCRDEstablished: storedVersions was a nil slice, JSON-marshaling\n  as null when spec.versions was missing/malformed instead of an empty\n  array like a real CRD's status always has. Also add a fallback to a\n  legacy apiextensions.k8s.io/v1beta1-style single spec.version string\n  when the v1 spec.versions list isn't present.\n- TestOverlay_CRDEstablishedOnCreate: the docstring claimed coverage of\n  both Established and NamesAccepted conditions, but only Established\n  was asserted. Added an explicit NamesAccepted=True check, plus a new\n  test covering both storedVersions fallbacks above.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(server): default acceptedNames to {} for a malformed CRD spec.names\n\nensureCRDEstablished's storedVersions was already fixed to be [] rather\nthan null when spec.versions is missing/malformed; acceptedNames had\nthe same gap when spec.names can't be decoded — a real CRD's\nstatus.acceptedNames is never omitted, matching the same fidelity\nprinciple. Flagged in a low-confidence Copilot re-review comment;\nNamesAccepted/storedVersions in the same comment were stale (already\nfixed in d06020a).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(server): test the legacy spec.version CRD shape against its real v1beta1 endpoint\n\nThe \"legacy v1beta1-style spec.version\" subtest posted a body using\nspec.version without spec.versions — the apiextensions.k8s.io/v1beta1\nCRD shape — but sent it to the v1 endpoint with apiVersion: .../v1. A\nreal v1 CRD requires spec.versions and would reject this body via\nOpenAPI validation, so the test wasn't exercising a body a real client\nwould ever actually send. Post it to the real v1beta1 endpoint instead;\nensureCRDEstablished keys only on group+resource, not version, so\nbehavior is unaffected — this just makes the test scenario honest.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
