          "distinct": true,
          "id": "424f80c7b6174f7f5df76e581c69165174e683a1",
          "message": "fix(ci): pin GoReleaser's current tag to the pushed ref explicitly (#194)\n\nCutting v0.5.1 immediately after v0.5.1-rc.4 (same commit, promoting an\nRC straight to stable) failed: GoReleaser resolves the \"current\" tag\nvia `git describe` on HEAD when it isn't told otherwise, which is\nambiguous when two tags point at the same commit. It picked\nv0.5.1-rc.4 again, then failed uploading duplicate-named assets to\nthat tag's already-published release — no v0.5.1 release was ever\ncreated.\n\nGORELEASER_CURRENT_TAG=${{ github.ref_name }} tells GoReleaser exactly\nwhich tag triggered this run, removing the ambiguity regardless of how\nmany tags share a commit.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-22T05:58:56-04:00",
          "tree_id": "219a8fa629642f46ccce487779954504e2a508a8",
