          "distinct": true,
          "id": "1b1edc844469e6e39d56d784ff7bdcae1bc74fee",
          "message": "fix(server): register a CRD's discovery entry when created via the overlay (#195)\n\n* fix(server): register a CRD's discovery entry when created via the overlay\n\nA CRD created at runtime (e.g. `istioctl install`) synthesized its\nEstablished status but never registered the type it defines with the\nstore's discovery metadata, which is otherwise a snapshot built once\nfrom the capture archive at startup. kubectl get crd worked (a plain\nobject read), but kubectl api-resources / istioctl analyze — which\nwalk /apis and /apis/<group>/<version> — never saw the new type.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(server): merge overlay-registered CRD types into captured discovery docs\n\nCopilot review of the CRD discovery fix found that a real capture almost\nalways records /apis and /apis/<group>/<version> unconditionally (see\nthe capture engine's fetchDiscovery), so tryServeFromStore was serving\nthat frozen document verbatim and shadowing any group/resource a CRD\nregistered via the overlay afterward — the runtime registration never\ntook effect for the common case.\n\nDiscovery handlers for /apis, /apis/<group>, and /apis/<group>/<version>\nnow surgically append any group/version/resource the overlay registered\nthat the captured document doesn't already list, leaving every\npre-existing entry as the exact bytes capture recorded (so an\nalready-captured resource's richer verbs/fields aren't clobbered by a\nfull re-synthesis). Read-only replay (no overlay) is unaffected — it\nkeeps serving captured documents byte-for-byte.\n\nAlso fixes a second review finding: an empty/unrecognized CRD\nspec.scope was treated as namespaced=true instead of being skipped,\nwhich could have overwritten mergeResourceInfo's authoritative\nnamespaced flag with a wrong default.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(server): merge new CRD versions into already-known /apis groups; skip discovery registration when kind is missing\n\nSecond round of Copilot review on the CRD discovery fix:\n\n- groupVersionsByGroup's exclude set was keyed by group name alone, so\n  a CRD adding a new served version to a group /apis already listed\n  (e.g. a second Istio CRD introducing v1beta1 under\n  networking.istio.io, which already had v1 captured) never showed up\n  in /apis at all — only in /apis/<group> and /apis/<group>/<version>.\n  tryServeAPIGroupListFromStore now also merges new versions into an\n  already-known group's own versions array (mergeVersionsIntoGroup),\n  not just wholesale-appending entirely new groups.\n\n- registerCRDResourceInfo now skips registration entirely when\n  spec.names.kind is missing, instead of letting mergeResourceInfo\n  fall through to the resourceToKind depluralization heuristic — that\n  heuristic is only reliable for built-in types and would likely guess\n  wrong for a CRD, polluting discovery with a made-up Kind.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* perf(server): hoist a single Resources() snapshot in tryServeAPIGroupListFromStore\n\nAvoid copying the whole resourceInfo map under lock on every group in\nthe loop; take one snapshot up front and reuse it for both the\nper-group version merge and the new-group append.\n\n* fix(server): reject JSON null in mergeJSONArrayField instead of nil map/slice\n\njson.Unmarshal into a map or slice succeeds with a nil result and no\nerror when the source is a literal \"null\" — so a captured document\nthat is (or has a field that is) JSON null was being treated as valid,\nand a later write into that nil map would panic. Reject both cases\nexplicitly so callers fall back to serving the captured bytes verbatim.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
