          "distinct": true,
          "id": "766f81ebaa3cc6c2cb1812b14868eb12a5ce8fa5",
          "message": "docs(examples): add self-contained worked examples for common use cases (#196)\n\n* docs(examples): add self-contained worked examples for common use cases\n\nAdd four runnable examples under examples/ (basic-workloads,\nmulti-namespace, crash-loop, rolling-update), each with a pre-recorded\ncapture, the config.yaml used to produce it, and a README walking through\nwhat to try. Adds an examples/README.md index and points the existing\ngeneric examples/k8shark.yaml at it.\n\nCloses #65\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(examples): address Copilot review feedback on #196\n\n- Point each config.yaml's output at its own examples/<name>/capture.kshrk\n  path so the documented \"run from repo root\" recapture command overwrites\n  the checked-in archive instead of writing to the repo root.\n- Fix a dead docs/config.md anchor in crash-loop's README.\n- Put kshrk on PATH in examples/README.md's quick start and use it\n  consistently instead of mixing ./kshrk and kshrk.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(examples): add auto-discovery worked example\n\nAdd a fifth example demonstrating `resources: - all: true`: a config with no\ngroup/version/resource entries that discovers every resource type in a\nnamespace at capture time, including a toy Widget CRD alongside built-in\nresources. Scoped to one namespace via `namespaces:` so it stays contained\non a shared cluster. Chains from rolling-update and adds an index row.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-22T18:18:55-04:00",
